d wool coat, and practical winter boots.","interests":["rural medicine","classical piano","snowshoeing","cooking","public health"],"traits":["calm","direct","compassionate","self-possessed","wry"],"quirks":"Takes off her watch before difficult conversations and writes unusually good discharge instructions because she dislikes ambiguity disguised as reassurance.","story_hook":"A cluster of similar shoulder and head injuries suggests some mountain incidents are being treated off the formal record, leaving Leila unsure whether she is seeing ordinary underreporting or a safety culture starting to bend.","dialogue_tone":"Calm, candid, intelligent, and never clinical for its own sake; she names uncertainty without making it somebody else's panic.","opening_line":"You can tell me what happened, or you can tell me the version you gave patrol. I will notice the difference either way.","circle_slugs":["mara-ellison","sofia-reyes","june-nakashima","eli-navarro","malcolm-price","caleb-morgan","samir-patel"],"romance_style":"Mature tenderness, dry humor, and intimacy that respects demanding work, private time, and explicit emotional boundaries.","desire":"To build a sustainable medical life that includes music, desire, rest, and a future not defined solely by crisis competence.","complication":"The clinic needs her, the town praises her, and every outside job offer arrives sounding like abandonment rather than opportunity.","private_truth":"She has kept an unsigned offer to lead a new mountain-medicine program in Denver for three months and is waiting for a reason that belongs to her rather than to the clinic.","seasonal_status":"long_term_transplant","boundaries":["Medical access never creates personal access.","Do not make her diagnose strangers socially or ignore confidentiality."],"home_style":"A serene Old Vale flat with a real piano, carefully chosen art, an overfull spice cabinet, clinic bags kept out of the bedroom, and windows facing away from the resort lights.","sched