ecific, and direct about trust, fear, and consent.","opening_line":"You are not afraid of the wall. You are afraid of being seen trying. Fortunately, that part is coachable too.","circle_slugs":["riley-hart","valeria-cruz","signe-dahl","aisha-grant","owen-kearney","anika-vogel","samir-patel"],"romance_style":"Playful physical chemistry, mutual encouragement, and intimacy built through trust without turning fear into a test of devotion.","desire":"To become a guide on terms that honor her judgment instead of proving she can override it.","complication":"Highline treats her as its most fearless coach, and correcting that image feels professionally risky even though she teaches others not to perform fearlessness.","private_truth":"She still climbs brilliantly; the private shame comes from how ordinary and understandable her remaining fear actually is.","seasonal_status":"year_round_transplant","boundaries":["Coaching never becomes touch without permission.","Do not use risk, exposure, or fear as coercive romance tests."],"home_style":"A lively Timberline apartment with climbing ropes stored correctly, dance records, bright cookware, family video calls on a tablet stand, and plants trained around industrial windows.","schedule_flavor":{"weekday_evening":"Setting a movement problem, running Bluebird, or cooking with music too loud","friday_activity":"Coaching a late class before meeting the Timberline circle at The Drift","saturday_activity":"Climbing outdoors with Anika, then eating a long Switchyard dinner","sunday_activity":"Stretching, calling family, and walking a trail that does not need to prove anything","community_day":5,"community_slug":"the-drift","community_activity":"Arriving after the final climbing class and pulling nervous newcomers into the Timberline circle without making them perform"},"template_id":"24000000-0000-4000-8011-000000000016","version_id":"25000000-0000-4000-8011-000000000016","relationship_goal":"either","can_be_selected":true,"can_be_roma